IMPORTING AND EXPORTING DATA FROM VARIOUS DATABASES
AIM:
To study the importing and exporting of data from different databases using MySQL, Hive and Sqoop.
PROCEDURE:
SQOOP is used to transfer data between MySQL and Hadoop (HDFS).
- Importing: Transferring data from MySQL to Hive/HDFS.
- Exporting: Transferring data from Hive/HDFS to MySQL.
A. Importing Data from MySQL to HDFS
Step 1: Login into MySQL.
mysql -u root -p


Step 2: Create a database, table and insert data.
CREATE DATABASE student;

USE student;

CREATE TABLE details (
    id INT,
    name VARCHAR(30),
    age INT
);

INSERT INTO details VALUES
(1,'Arun',20),
(2,'Bala',21),
(3,'Ravi',22);

SELECT * FROM details;


Step 3: Create a table in Hive.
CREATE DATABASE student;

USE student;

CREATE TABLE details (
    id INT,
    name STRING,
    age INT
);


Step 4: Run the Sqoop import command.
sqoop import \
--connect jdbc:mysql://localhost:3306/student \
--username root \
--password cloudera \
--table details \
--hive-import \
--hive-table student.details \
--m 1


Step 5: Check whether the data is imported successfully.
SELECT * FROM student.details;


B. Exporting Data from HDFS to MySQL
Step 1: Create a database and table in Hive.
CREATE DATABASE company;

USE company;

CREATE TABLE employee (
    id INT,
    name STRING,
    salary INT
);


Step 2: Insert data into the Hive table.
INSERT INTO employee VALUES
(1,'Arun',15000),
(2,'Bala',20000),
(3,'Ravi',25000);


Step 3: Create a database and table in MySQL.
CREATE DATABASE company;

USE company;

CREATE TABLE employee (
    id INT,
    name VARCHAR(30),
    salary INT
);


Step 4: Run the Sqoop export command.
sqoop export \
--connect jdbc:mysql://localhost:3306/company \
--username root \
--password cloudera \
--table employee \
--export-dir /user/hive/warehouse/company.db/employee \
--m 1


Step 5: Check whether the data is exported successfully.
SELECT * FROM employee;


RESULT:
Thus, the importing and exporting of data between MySQL, Hive and HDFS using Sqoop was studied and successfully verified.
